      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits on the historic Camino Real, the Royal Road that followed the Rio Grande and linked trading centers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bosquefarmsnm.gov/residents/village-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1700s Spanish settlers called the area Bosque del Pino, meaning Forest Pines, before it became Bosque Farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bosque_Farms%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dairy farming survived poor soil and became the main industry through the 1960s, shaping the community’s economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bosque_Farms%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Bosque Farms incorporated as an official village in 1974, marking its transition from a resettlement project to a self‑governed community.",
